// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'section'
//
// FlatData written as a bare block where the `content:` STRING should be. This is the single
// most misleading thing about the ###ExternalFormat section: FlatData looks like a section
// grammar -- it has `section`, `Record`, typed fields, braces -- and it is not one. It is a
// self-contained sub-grammar whose entire input is the QUOTED content of a schema.
//
// `content:` is `SCHEMA_CONTENT COLON STRING SEMI_COLON`. Nothing else. A rewritten parser
// that recognises FlatData as a nested block -- the obvious reading of the positive
// fixture's escaped one-liner -- accepts a shape legend-engine has no rule for.
###ExternalFormat
SchemaSet fixture::neg::FlatDataOutsideString
{
   format: FlatData;
   schemas: [
      {
         id: primary;
         content:
            section people: DelimitedWithHeadings
            {
               scope.untilEof;
               delimiter: ',';

               Record
               {
                  NAME : STRING;
               }
            };
      }
   ];
}
